# Autonomous wave (opt-in)

Full contract: [`.eteller/memory/workflows/autonomous-wave.md`](.eteller/memory/workflows/autonomous-wave.md).

## When it applies

Only after an **explicit** user steer for this wave/session (“autonomous wave”, “modo autónomo”, or start-wave that also says: review prompts in chat + launch review subagents + merge when reviews pass + compile/Setup for IT). Record the steer in integration `history/` + `worksession.txt`.

Default eteller still applies until then (prompts only; no auto-review; no auto-merge).

## Hard gates that never lift

- Ask for **story** after base+integration
- Ask before **each** wave start
- Ask before **promote base**
- Never start wave N+1 automatically
- Never skip `approved` / `ux_ready` gates
- Implementer never self-approves

## While autonomous is on

1. **Orchestrator** stays in the user chat; launch reviewer/UXReviewer as background `Task` subagents.
2. Default review models: `gpt-5.6-terra-medium` (override only if user names another listed slug). Implementers default `cursor-grok-4.5-high`.
3. Always write prompt files under `integration/<repo>/.eteller/prompts/` **and** paste a copyable fenced textbox in chat.
4. On `approved: true` → launch UXReview the same way.
5. If the steer included merge-on-pass → merge when both gates are true; pull **integration/**; rollup `ux_review/wave-N.md`.
6. When **all** wave slots are merged → Release build / installer in **integration/**; report the artifact path; **stop** and ask before promote base / next wave.

## Conflict merges

Keep slot `.eteller/*` (ours). Combine product files so sibling wave features are not dropped.
